 "scale_note": "frame: the holes of ideal hexagonal close packing (the twinned octet) at ball spacing sqrt2 in orthonormal rational coordinates (close-packed layers perpendicular to (1, 1, 1): a1 = (1, -1, 0), a2 = (1, 0, -1), c = (4/3)(1, 1, 1); the census cell hcpholes mapped by x = L f); the #56/#57 values are at ball spacing 1: divide lengths by sqrt2 and volumes by 2 sqrt2 (the frame of Samson and Delilah, dicto-samson). Weights w_oct = 0, w_tet = lambda as in the census (#53 units, ball spacing 1). The piece is moved so that its hole (site) is at the origin. Lahdeli: the octahedral hole (2/3, 2/3, 1/4) of the census cell (site 0) at lambda = t, the equal-volume point. At this frame volume 2/3 = sqrt2/6 at ball spacing 1 (#56: two octahedral and four tetrahedral pieces in the cell of volume sqrt2).",
